arc-ternary-triton

This project builds on the Flint-40B model (ternary PQ2_0 2-bit mixture-of-experts), which is licensed under
the Apache License 2.0. Trained multiplier files derived from it are published at
https://huggingface.co/TheSanchezian/Ternary-Flint-40B-Intel-Arc

This repository contains code only; it does not include the model weights.

Modifications and additions in this repository:
- Triton unpack kernels for PQ2_0 expert weights (kernels/ternary_unpack.py), bit-identical to the torch unpack.
- A PyTorch XPU training implementation of Flint-40B that trains only the per-expert-row scale multipliers
  (trainer/flint_torch.py, trainer/flint_train.py, trainer/flint_supervisor.py), with batched expert groups,
  expert-sorted grouping, routing reuse, one host-to-device copy per layer, and blocked attention.
- trainer/flint_rt.py: GGUF reader / PQ2_0 layout helpers and an OpenCL inference runtime, used by the trainer.
- Windows Triton setup scripts and notes (setup/).

Written and trained with help from Claude (Anthropic).
